{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CeuqCenMcWVRddzzQp6Mw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a complete understanding of the codebase. Let me summarize my findings:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Shipment model at `Shipment.kt:1-34` with ShipmentStatus enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- Repository at `ShipmentRepository.kt:1-27` provides save, findById, existsById methods\n- Controller at `ShipmentController.kt:1-56` implements POST create, GET by id, and GET list endpoints\n- Exception types at `ApiExceptions.kt:1-31`: ResourceNotFoundException (404), ConflictException (409)\n- Error codes at `ApiError.kt:31-37`: Currently SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND and SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS\n- GlobalExceptionHandler at `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:1-30` converts ApiException to response envelope\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n- POST endpoints return `ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED).body(object)`\n- GET endpoints return object directly or throw ResourceNotFoundException\n- Conflicts use ConflictException with 409 status\n- All error responses wrapped in `ApiError` envelope with code and message\n- Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath for assertions\n\n**Affected files (must change):**\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` - Add POST confirm endpoint\n2. `ApiError.kt` - Add new ErrorCode for invalid shipment state (SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS or similar)\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - Add tests for confirm endpoint behavior\n\n**Risks:**\n- Adding a new error code changes the ErrorCode enum (already in the repository's API)\n- Must ensure idempotent behavior for double-confirm calls\n- Needs to handle CANCELLED state with 409\n\n**Open questions:**\nNone - all requirements are clearly specified.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **`ApiError.kt`**: Add a new error code `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` to the ErrorCode enum. This represents when a shipment operation conflicts with its current state (e.g., confirming a cancelled shipment).\n\n2. **`ShipmentController.kt`**: Add a new endpoint `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` that:\n   - Takes the shipmentId from path variable\n   - Calls repository.findById() to get the shipment\n   - Throws ResourceNotFoundException if not found\n   - If status is CREATED, updates it to CONFIRMED and saves via repository.save()\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, returns the shipment unchanged (idempotent)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throws ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS\n   - Returns ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.OK).body(confirmedShipment)\n\n3. **`ShipmentControllerTest.kt`**: Add four new tests:\n   - Confirm a created shipment moves it to confirmed and returns the updated object\n   - Confirm an already confirmed shipment succeeds without changes (idempotent)\n   - Confirm a cancelled shipment returns 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS error code\n   - Confirm a non-existent shipment returns 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND error code\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Using `@PutMapping` instead of `@PostMapping`: Rejected because the requirement explicitly asks for POST, and POST is semantically correct for an action endpoint (non-idempotent in HTTP semantics, but made idempotent at the domain level). The requirement's explicit POST instruction takes precedence.\n- Throwing ValidationException for CANCELLED state: Rejected because ConflictException with 409 is the correct HTTP status for \"request conflicts with current state\" per ApiExceptions.kt comment.\n- Creating a separate service layer: Rejected because the OrderController and existing ShipmentController don't use one; consistency with existing architecture is required.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n*Case 1: Confirm CREATED shipment*\n- Read: repository.findById(shipmentId) → Shipment{status=CREATED}\n- Write: repository.save(Shipment{status=CONFIRMED})\n- Return: ResponseEntity.status(200).body(Shipment{status=CONFIRMED})\n- Caller receives: 200 OK with updated shipment\n\n*Case 2: Confirm already CONFIRMED shipment (idempotent)*\n- Read: repository.findById(shipmentId) → Shipment{status=CONFIRMED}\n- Write: repository.save(Shipment{status=CONFIRMED}) (no actual change)\n- Return: ResponseEntity.status(200).body(Shipment{status=CONFIRMED})\n- Caller receives: 200 OK with shipment unchanged\n\n*Case 3: Confirm CANCELLED shipment*\n- Read: repository.findById(shipmentId) → Shipment{status=CANCELLED}\n- Write: None\n- Throw: ConflictException(SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS, \"Cannot confirm a cancelled shipment\")\n- GlobalExceptionHandler converts to: 409 CONFLICT with ApiError{code=SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS, message=\"...\"}\n- Caller receives: 409 CONFLICT error response\n\n*Case 4: Confirm non-existent shipment*\n- Read: repository.findById(shipmentId) → null\n- Write: None\n- Throw: ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, \"No shipment with id '...'\")\n- GlobalExceptionHandler converts to: 404 NOT_FOUND with ApiError{code=SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, message=\"...\"}\n- Caller receives: 404 NOT_FOUND error response\n\n**Test strategy:**\n1. Test confirm CREATED → moves to CONFIRMED and persists: Create S-1, confirm it, verify status changed to CONFIRMED\n2. Test confirm CONFIRMED is idempotent: Create S-2, confirm twice, verify second confirm succeeds with 200 OK and no change\n3. Test confirm CANCELLED returns 409: Manually save CANCELLED shipment to repository, confirm it, expect 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS code\n4. Test confirm non-existent returns 404: Confirm unknown shipment, expect 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":865,"cache_read_input_tokens":16100,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":865},"output_tokens"